			"25": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "STACK\n\nThe Stack node is a value collector similar to the Ring Buffer and Buffer nodes.\n\nThe Stack node will fill up each time a value is pushed.\nThe value is placed on top of the stack (index 0), all other values are shifted up and removed if they exceed the size of the stack.\n\nThe Pop trigger will remove the top of the stack, reseting it to 0 and the Reset trigger will set the entire stack back to 0."
					}
				},
